course: dictionary
lesson: 11776
title: Short forms in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are not real words at all. They are just letters that stand for longer words, and one word can have several meanings. «bb» is one of these. To work out which meaning fits, look at the words around it.
explain: «Bye bye, bb, see you at school!» This is a text message, and bb is short for bye bye. Check your meaning in the sentence: bye bye makes sense as a goodbye, so it fits.
explain: «The pencil was a soft BB, so the line went dark.» On a pencil, BB means very soft and dark. The clues are pencil and dark line. Here BB is not a word for a pet or a goodbye.
explain: «A BB gun can hurt your eyes, so it is never a toy.» Here BB means a small metal pellet from an air gun. The warning tells you something important: a BB gun is not a toy, and you should never point one at anyone.
fact: BB and bb are abbreviations, which means short forms made from letters.
fact: In texting, «bb» means bye bye or babe, a pet name.
fact: On pencils, BB means very soft and dark, and more B means softer.
fact: A BB is a small round metal pellet fired from an air gun called a BB gun.
fact: BB guns can injure eyes, so they are not toys and should never be pointed at anyone.
exercise: «Bye for now, bb, see you at school!» What does bb mean in this text message? | Very soft and dark | *Bye bye | A type of bed | A small metal pellet
exercise: «The art teacher gave Ana a BB pencil for the dark shadows.» What does BB mean on a pencil? | Broken | Brand new | *Very soft and dark | Very hard and pale
exercise: «BB guns can injure eyes, so never point one at anyone.» What is the safe lesson here? | BB guns are toys for playing games | Point a BB gun at a friend to test it | *A BB gun is not a toy, so never point it at anyone | Keep BB guns in your pocket for later
test: «Love you, bb! Night night.» What does bb mean in this text? | A small metal pellet | *Baby, a pet name | Big Brother | Very dark
test: Which pencil is softer, a B or a 2B? | *2B | Neither is soft | B | They are the same
exam: Which sentence uses BB to mean a small metal pellet? | «Pass me the BB pencil.» | «Bb, see you soon!» | *«A BB gun is not a toy.» | «Love you, bb.»
